WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.090
Our raw data is twelve parquet files, one per month of 2025.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.460
They are too big for git, so they stay in a data folder that git ignores.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:19.324
DuckDB reads them in place, and a source, in sources dot yml, gives them a name dbt can use.

00:00:20.274 --> 00:00:24.991
The second file is small: a lookup of the 265 taxi zones.

00:00:25.271 --> 00:00:27.959
Small CSV files like this one are seeds.

00:00:28.239 --> 00:00:32.041
They live in the repository, and dbt loads them as tables.

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:37.173
The files come from the New York City Taxi and Limousine Commission website.

00:00:37.453 --> 00:00:43.632
Under 2025, download Green Taxi Trip Records for each month, January to December.

00:00:43.912 --> 00:00:45.400
The links are in the description.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:51.044
Further down the same page, download the Taxi Zone Lookup Table, as CSV.

00:00:51.994 --> 00:00:55.070
In Studio, open the nyc taxi project.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.580
Right-click the project, choose New Folder, and call it data.

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:03.886
Inside data, make a folder called raw.

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:13.178
Now move the twelve parquet files into data, raw, and the zone lookup CSV into seeds.

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.564
Refresh the explorer, and there they are.

00:01:16.514 --> 00:01:19.003
Next, tell dbt about the raw files.

00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:22.810
Right-click models, New File, and call it sources dot yml.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.146
A source called raw, with a short description.

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.043
It has one table, green trips: one row per green taxi trip.

00:01:32.993 --> 00:01:38.578
And where the table lives: external location, a read parquet call over all twelve files.

00:01:38.858 --> 00:01:44.190
Union by name lines up the columns, even if a month's file has them in a different order.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.069
Save.

00:01:46.019 --> 00:01:47.773
Does dbt find the data?

00:01:48.053 --> 00:01:53.000
In the command box, type dbt show, inline, and a query that counts the rows of the source.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.088
Press Enter.

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:10.116
dbt turns the source into the read parquet call, and DuckDB counts five hundred ninety-one thousand, three hundred seventy-five trips, in 2025.

00:02:11.066 --> 00:02:12.094
Now the Git tab.

00:02:12.374 --> 00:02:16.235
Only two files changed: sources dot yml and the CSV.

00:02:16.515 --> 00:02:21.029
The parquet files are not here, because the gitignore leaves out the data folder.

00:02:21.979 --> 00:02:27.115
Stage all, type a message, declare the raw trips source and add the zone lookup, and commit.

00:02:30.669 --> 00:02:32.085
Then click Sync Changes.

00:02:32.365 --> 00:02:34.318
Studio pushes the commit to GitHub.

00:02:35.769 --> 00:02:41.691
On GitHub, the repository now has the models and seeds folders, and the latest commit message.

00:02:42.641 --> 00:02:46.045
To recap: the trip files sit in data raw, outside git.

00:02:46.325 --> 00:02:47.711
The zone lookup is a seed.

00:02:47.991 --> 00:02:53.837
And sources dot yml names the raw files, raw dot green trips, which dbt can read.

00:02:54.117 --> 00:02:56.482
Next, we build our first model on top of it.
